From: "vincent.yen" <vincent.yen@mitaccomputing.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 01:08:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add redfish event log

- Firmware update supports the following Redfish MessageId
  - OpenBMC.0.5.FirmwareUpdateStarted
  - OpenBMC.0.5.FirmwareUpdateCompleted
  - OpenBMC.0.5.FirmwareUpdateFailed
  - OpenBMC.0.5.BMCBootReason

- Since the BMC update will trigger a reboot, the following procedures need to be performed.
  - phosphor-software-manager
    - /var/log/bmcFirmwareUpdateInprogress Record the image version to be updated by the firmware.
  - BMC shutdown -> update:
    - Read the firmware update image version from /var/log/bmcFirmwareUpdateInprogress to trigger event log, then delete the file.
    - Record the image version and update result to /var/log/bmcFirmwareUpdateFinish
  - BMC reboot
  - phosphor-software-manager
    - If /var/log/bmcFirmwareUpdateFinish is present, record any pending Redfish event logs, then delete the file.

- Test:
  Execute BMC/BIOS firmware update, expecting Redfish event log to be generated
  curl -k -u root:0penBmc https://$BMC/redfish/v1/Systems/system/LogServices/EventLog/Entries

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [No upstream maintenance]
